    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d344">

                <pb facs="0508" n="416" xml:id="pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2393</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-29T14:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1918, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 30, 12.50
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4904. Through an entirely reliable propagandist [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >spokesman?</hi>], the Turkish Minister here has conveyed the information
                    that he has been instructed by his Government to see the American representative
                    and to say that Turkish Government is very desirous of renewing friendly and
                    diplomatic relations with the United States. Please instruct. In view of your
                        2230<anchor n="1" xml:id="d344-f1"/> I have repeated above to Colonel
                        House at Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bliss</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
